  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhen a `<script>` element is first connected, the type is fixed at that time, regardless of whether the 'type' attribute changes after that point. So a classic script that has been connected cannot be converted to an import map and vice versa by changing the `type` attribute, even if it's removed and reconnected. This behavior makes sense and probably shouldn't change. \n\nBut it seems that the [specification for HTMLScriptElement](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-script-element) needs to account for this behavior, and we probably need more WPTs. \n\nI have a CL out to add WPT's for Import Maps vs classic scripts, but we will probably need more for the other script types: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7004710",
